  "faqs": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "question": "What is the buying process?",
      "answer": "The buying process involves: 1) Property search and shortlisting, 2) Site visits and evaluation, 3) Price negotiation, 4) Legal verification of documents, 5) Booking and agreement signing, 6) Home loan processing (if applicable), 7) Registration and stamp duty payment, 8) Possession and handover. Our team at H.O.M Advisory guides you through every step.",
      "category": "buying",
      "order": 1,
      "isActive": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "question": "How do I schedule a property viewing?",
      "answer": "You can schedule a property viewing by: 1) Clicking the 'Schedule Visit' button on any property page, 2) Calling us at (555) 123-4567, 3) Filling out the contact form on our website, or 4) Sending us an email at info@homadvisory.com. Our team will confirm and arrange the visit at your convenience.",
      "category": "general",
      "order": 2,
      "isActive": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "question": "What documents do I need to buy a property?",
      "answer": "To buy a property in India, you typically need: PAN Card, Aadhaar Card, Passport-size photos, Bank statements (last 6 months), Salary slips (last 3 months) or ITR (for self-employed), Property documents from seller including Title Deed, Encumbrance Certificate, Khata Certificate, and RERA registration details. Our legal team helps verify all documents.",
      "category": "buying",
      "order": 3,
      "isActive": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "question": "How long does it take to close a deal?",
      "answer": "The timeline varies depending on several factors. For a ready-to-move property with clear documents, the process from booking to registration typically takes 30-45 days. If a home loan is involved, add another 15-20 days for loan processing. For under-construction properties, you make staged payments per the builder's schedule.",
      "category": "buying",
      "order": 4,
      "isActive": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "question": "What are the additional costs beyond the property price?",
      "answer": "Beyond the base property price, you should budget for: Registration charges (1% of property value in Karnataka), Stamp duty (5% for properties above Rs 45 lakhs), GST (5% for under-construction, 0% for ready-to-move), Legal fees, Home loan processing fees, Maintenance deposit, and Parking charges (if not included). H.O.M Advisory provides a complete cost breakdown upfront.",
      "category": "buying",
      "order": 5,
      "isActive": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "question": "How does H.O.M Advisory help with home loans?",
      "answer": "H.O.M Advisory partners with leading banks and NBFCs to offer you the best home loan rates. We help with: Pre-approval of loan eligibility, Document preparation, Application submission to multiple banks, Rate negotiation, and EMI structuring. Our service is completely free for homebuyers.",
      "category": "home-loan",
      "order": 6,
      "isActive": true
    }
  ],
  "articles": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Premium Apartments in Mumbai: Top 5 Luxury Towers",
      "slug": "premium-apartments-mumbai-top-luxury-towers",
      "excerpt": "Discover the most exclusive luxury apartment towers in Mumbai, from South Mumbai's iconic addresses to the emerging skyline of Lower Parel and Worli.",
      "content": "Mumbai has always been the epicenter of luxury real estate in India. From the iconic Marine Drive to the bustling Bandra-Worli Sea Link corridor, the city offers some of the most prestigious addresses in the country.\n\n## 1. World One, Lower Parel\nStanding at 442 meters, World One is one of the tallest residential towers in the world. It offers 3, 4, and 5 BHK apartments with breathtaking views of the Mumbai skyline.\n\n## 2. Palais Royale, Worli\nThis ultra-luxury tower features private elevators, Italian marble throughout, and an infinity pool on the 35th floor.\n\n## Key Takeaways\n- Mumbai's luxury market continues to grow at 8-10% annually\n- Sea-facing properties command a 40-60% premium\n- New-age luxury includes smart home features and sustainability",
      "image": "https://placehold.co/800x400/goldenrod/white?text=Mumbai+Luxury+Towers",
      "category": "market-trends",
      "tags": ["mumbai", "luxury", "apartments", "investment"],
      "author": "H.O.M Advisory Team",
      "publishedAt": "2025-12-01T10:00:00Z",
      "isActive": true,
      "seoTitle": "Top 5 Luxury Apartment Towers in Mumbai | H.O.M Advisory",
      "seoDescription": "Explore Mumbai's most premium luxury apartment towers. Detailed guide to the best high-rise living options in India's financial capital."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Discover Elegance in Bangalore's Most Sought-After Villas",
      "slug": "elegance-bangalore-sought-after-villas",
      "excerpt": "Bangalore's villa market is booming. Explore the best villa communities that combine luxury living with nature, from Whitefield to North Bangalore.",
      "content": "Bangalore's villa market has seen tremendous growth, driven by remote work flexibility and the desire for spacious living. Here's our curated guide to the finest villa communities.\n\n## Why Villas in Bangalore?\n- Work-from-home has made space a priority\n- Bangalore's pleasant climate is perfect for villa living\n- Appreciation rates of 12-15% in premium locations\n\n## Top Villa Communities\n1. **Prestige Lakeside Habitat** - 102-acre township in Varthur\n2. **Total Environment** - Boutique villas in JP Nagar\n3. **Embassy Pristine** - Luxury villas on Devanahalli Road\n\n## Investment Outlook\nVillas in Bangalore have shown consistent appreciation, especially in the north and east corridors near the airport and IT hubs.",
      "image": "https://placehold.co/800x400/goldenrod/white?text=Bangalore+Villas",
      "category": "buying-guide",
      "tags": ["bangalore", "villas", "luxury", "investment"],
      "author": "H.O.M Advisory Team",
      "publishedAt": "2025-11-15T10:00:00Z",
      "isActive": true,
      "seoTitle": "Best Luxury Villas in Bangalore 2025 | H.O.M Advisory",
      "seoDescription": "Complete guide to Bangalore's finest villa communities. From Whitefield to North Bangalore, find your dream villa."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Exclusive Penthouses: 4 Homes with Rooftop Sky Lounges",
      "slug": "exclusive-penthouses-rooftop-sky-lounges",
      "excerpt": "Experience the pinnacle of luxury living with these exclusive penthouses featuring private rooftop sky lounges, infinity pools, and panoramic city views.",
      "content": "Penthouses represent the ultimate in urban luxury. These homes in the sky offer unparalleled views, exclusive amenities, and the kind of privacy that ground-level homes simply cannot match.\n\n## What Makes a Penthouse Special?\n- Private terraces with panoramic views\n- Double-height living areas\n- Personal pools and sky lounges\n- Dedicated elevator access\n\n## Top Penthouses in India\n1. **The Imperial, Delhi** - 12,000 sqft penthouse with private helipad\n2. **World One, Mumbai** - Sky villa at 400m height\n3. **Embassy One, Bangalore** - Penthouse with 360-degree views\n4. **DLF Camellias, Gurgaon** - Ultra-luxury penthouse with butler service\n\n## Price Range\nPenthouses in India's top cities range from Rs 10 Cr to Rs 100+ Cr, depending on location and amenities.",
